body:
The `AGENTS.md`-hygiene surface of the distributed agent-builder template `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md` (product source embedded via `include_str!` and installed by `apg init` into `~/.opencode/agents/`). It carries:
- the `AGENTS.md` frontmatter write grant: the template's `edit:` block (`"*": deny`) allows the repo-root `AGENTS.md` ALONGSIDE `.opencode/agents/**` and `opencode.json`, resolved against the session workspace root (the main checkout), with NO `apg/.worktrees/*/AGENTS.md` mirror and no broader glob (`*.md`/`**`) — so the hygiene instruction is executable;
- the hygiene rules: `AGENTS.md` must not contradict the distributed-agent rules and must not duplicate the canonical change-set process (owned solely by `codebase-navigator`, `requirements.requirement.navigator-staged-flow`) — where it restates the process, remove or repoint it to reference the navigator;
- the NON-DESTRUCTIVE merge rule (all repo-specific content — build gates, test tiers, pipeline, release steps — preserved);
- the only-when-present rule (`AGENTS.md` is optional per project; never manufactured);
- the universality statement (every apg project; the apg repo's local `build-implementer` also touching `AGENTS.md` is a local arrangement, not a universal rule).

Deliberately a NARROW owner distinct from `solution.component.agent-builder-prompt` (the same file's broad surface enumeration), so that `rust.apg.plan_cmd.verify.coverage_check` maps this requirement's coverage 1:1 to the single edited file `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md` — the component's ONLY `implemented-by` target. Two components sharing one code target is established practice here (`solution.component.codebase-navigator-prompt` and `solution.component.navigator-prompt-guidance` already share `opencode-suite/agents/codebase-navigator.md`). Product source in `solution.container.opencode-suite`; the repo's own `.opencode/agents/**` and `AGENTS.md` are consumer artifacts never edited by a change-set.

implemented-by: `opencode-suite/agents/agent-builder.md`.
